Û fikrê rawdeyê te çawa hanî, te ev rawdeyek vekir ji
zarokan re?
 
And how did you come up with the kindergarten idea, to open
this kindergarten for the children?

122
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Ez bi xwe, min ehliyet te'lîm xwend.
 
I myself, I studied teaching qualification.

123
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Teba'en, zirûfên çêbûn me temam nekir, yanî. Zirûfên ... qe
nebe der Efrînê de me temam nekir.
 
Naturally, circumstances happened we didn't finish, I mean.
The circumstances ... at least in Afrin we didn't finish.

124
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:34,000
Bes me xwend yanî.
 
But we studied I mean.

125
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Min di gundên Efrînê, texrîben, ji pêşî ve ders dida.
 
I gave lessons in the villages of Afrin, approximately, from
the beginning.

126
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Ez çawa gundê Şêtarê bêjim.
 
How can I describe the village of Shetara.

127
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,000
Min di gundên din de jî ...
 
I also in other villages ...

128
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Me, tedrîskirinê de, xwe da kar ...
 
We engaged ourselves in teaching ...

129
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Xaseten gundan, gundên me li Efrînê.
 
Especially the villages, our villages in Afrin.

130
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:52,000
Û di gundê me de mu'elîm hebûn ... muwaselat nîn bûn.
 
And we had teachers in our village... there was no
transportation.

131
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Em bi xwe di wî demî de, mektebê de em bi peyatî diçûn.
 
We ourselves at that time, we went to school on foot.

132
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:59,000
Em çiqas westiyayî bin, mektebê de me bi peyatî diçû ...
heta weha em hatin.
 
No matter how tired we were, we walked to school ... until
we came like this.

133
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:02,000
Xwarina me li ser milê, me gund bi gund digeriya ...
 
Our food on our shoulders, we wandered from village to
village ...

134
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Ewe.
 
Yes.

135
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Me şîr û mast pir dixwar ...
 
We ate a lot of milk and yogurt ...

136
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Fe fe'len ez çûm tedrîskirinê.
 
So effectively I went into teaching.

137
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Ew feterk pir, pir xweş bû di jiyana min de.
 
That period was very, very nice in my life.

138
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Paşê em hatin mektebên Efrînê.
 
Then we came to the schools of Afrin.

139
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Min mektebek ehlî, xasma vekir.
 
I opened a private, special school.

140
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Ez bi xwe di nav de ... destpêka vekirina mekteba Asdîqa, ez
yekem mamoste bûm tê de.
 
I myself was in it ... the beginning of opening the Asdiqa
school, I was the first teacher there.

141
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Û piştre ez bûm nûnera mektebê.
 
And then I became the representative of the school.

142
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:35,000
Têkeliyek pir baş me çêkir.
 
We made a very good connection.

143
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:39,000
Texrîben feterk pir dirêj ez tê de bûm.
 
Approximately I was in it for a very long period.

144
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Xebreta me a rawdeyê, bi serahî, min ji mekteba Asdîqa girt.
 
Our kindergarten experience, frankly, I got it from Asdiqa
school.

145
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:48,000
Mamoste Riyad, xwediyê mektebê bû. Min xebreta xwe ya pir jê
wergirt.
 
Teacher Riyad, was the owner of the school. I got most of my
experience from him.

146
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Yanî rawde, ne wekî îbtîdaî ye.
 
I mean kindergarten, is not like primary.

147
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Yanî te'amulê qicikê rawdeyê, ne wek te'amulê qicikê îbtîdaî
ye. Be'tebarî zarok hesas in.
 
I mean dealing with a kindergarten child, is not like
dealing with a primary child. Considering children are
sensitive.

148
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Te'amulî wan, te'amulê...
 
Dealing with them, dealing...

149
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:02,000
Te zanî zarok tên rawdeyê xam in...
 
You know children come to kindergarten raw...

150
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Bes, heger te zanî te çawa sûlûkî wî îdare kir ...
 
But, if you knew how to manage their behavior ...

151
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:11,000
Dibe ku yê digirî heye, yê şermok heye ... yê înad dike
heye...
 
There might be one who cries, one who is shy ... one who is
stubborn...

152
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Û bi seraha nika em pir muşkîle dibînin nika.
 
And frankly now we see a lot of problems now.

153
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Em pir meseleya tewehud, di nav zarokan de dibînin.
 
We see a lot of autism issues, among the children.

154
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Pir çêbûye, xaseten di vê herbê de.
 
It has increased a lot, especially in this war.

155
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Yanî zarok tê bal me, em sivik dibînin...
 
I mean the child comes to us, we see it lightly...

156
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Ya rebî ev zarok çima weha ye?
 
Oh Lord why is this child like this?

157
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,000
Zimanê zarokan paş dikeve, ziman der nakeve...
 
Children's language is delayed, language doesn't come out...

158
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Halet pir çêdibin di nava me de, ku deng nake...
 
Cases happen a lot among us, that doesn't make a sound...

159
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Ev jî te'sîra telefonan e pir e...
 
This is also the influence of phones, it's a lot...

160
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:39,000
Fe rawde, bi rastî, telefonan ji destê wan dûr dixe.
 
So kindergarten, honestly, keeps phones away from their
hands.

161
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Wan dikişîne nav zarokan, da hevalên xwe bibîne...
 
Draws them among the children, so they can see their
friends...

162
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:45,000
Bi vî rengî bêtir tevlî dibe, têkel dibe...
 
This way they participate more, become more social...

163
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:49,000
Fa ev me'anata me di vê meselê de em dibînin ... heye.
 
So this suffering of ours in this issue we see ... exists.

164
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Fe vî fikrî, dema çêbûna rawdeyê, min xwest ...
 
So this idea, at the time of creating the kindergarten, I
wanted ...

165
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Ji ber wek mekteba Asdîqa halet pir derbas bûn...
 
Because like the Asdiqa school, cases passed by a lot...

166
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:04,000
Min xwest û min hez kir ... ku ev tiştên xebreta min berê
çêbûye, ez wê bixebitim.
 
I wanted and I liked ... that these things from my
experience that happened before, I put to work.

167
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Û wekî te dît, tu zarokên me, zarokên Efrînê, pêşkêş dikî.
 
And as you saw, you present our children, the children of
Afrin.

168
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,000
Serkeftin bê, mamoste.
 
May there be success, teacher.

169
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Sax bî mamoste. Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Thank you teacher. May God be pleased with you.

170
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Xwezîka her dem tu vî ezmûnî, derbasî nav van zarokan bikî.
 
I wish you always pass this experience on to these children.

171
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:23,000
Ehlen we sehlen... û qapî me jî her dem vekiriye, û çi wextî
...
 
Welcome... and our door is also always open, and any time
...

172
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Em spasiya te dikin, em gelekî serbilind in.
 
We thank you, we are very proud.

173
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,000
Sax bî mamoste, sax bî.
 
Thank you teacher, thank you.

174
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Me di van zarokan de hêvî dikir, ev nifş, belkî em mezin
bûn...
 
We hoped in these children, this generation, maybe we grew
up...

175
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Me di nav malê de ev şans nedît...
 
We didn't see this chance in the house...

176
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Rast e, rast e.
 
True, true.

177
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Û înşalah xweda wê rojên nebaş nede wan.
 
And God willing, God will not give them bad days.

178
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Bê guman ev tişt tesîreke mezin li ser zarokan dike.
 
Without a doubt this thing has a big impact on children.

179
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:45,000
Em dixwazin, wekî ku navê rawdeya me Hêvî ye.
 
We want, just as our kindergarten's name is Hevi (Hope).

180
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Yanî hêvî, nîşana hêviyê ye ... ku jiyaneke ronî ji van
zarokan re bibe.
 
I mean hope, is the symbol of hope ... that there will be a
bright life for these children.

181
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:52,000
Sax bî, mamoste.
 
Thank you, teacher.

182
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Ez spasiya te dikim.
 
I thank you.

183
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Sax bî.
 
Thank you.

184
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Ji kerema te, em piçek di nav rawdeyê de bigerin, ka ode,
hûn çawa mijûl dibin...
 
Please, let's walk a little inside the kindergarten, the
rooms, how you are occupied...

185
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Sax bî mamoste. Em hêvî dikin tu her wext ...
 
Thank you teacher. We hope you always ...

186
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Ku fîstîvalek an tiştek çêbû, tu werî ... tu yê me de'm
bikî.
 
If a festival or something happens, you come ... you will
support us.

187
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Înşalah, ez bi hêvî me ku ez carek din bêm, li seyrana we û
van zarokan, û ez daxwaza derketina we bikim.
 
God willing, I hope I come another time, to your picnic with
these children, and I request your outing.

188
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Înşalah. Spas ji te re.
 
God willing. Thank you.

189
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Bi rastî ez pir ji zarokan hez dikim, lewma xwe nêzîkî wan
dikim.
 
Honestly I love children a lot, that's why I get close to
them.

190
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Sax bî, sax bî.
 
Thank you, thank you.

191
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Wekî tu dizanî mekteba me ... pergala wê Erebî û Îngilîzî
ye.
 
As you know our school ... its system is Arabic and English.

192
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,000
Û ...
 
And ...

193
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Em dixwazin wekî ...
 
We want like ...

194
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:37,000
Navê rawde, em bikin Hêvî, ya Efrînê.
 
The kindergarten's name, to make it Hevi (Hope), of Afrin.

195
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Taybetmendiyek, wekî turasî bidinê.
 
To give it a special feature, like traditional.

196
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Fe lema belkî te dît, zarokan hinek kincên resmî li xwe
kiribûn ...
 
So that's why maybe you saw, some children were wearing
formal clothes ...

197
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Ev kincên Kurdî ne. Zarokên ji parêzgehên din jî li vir
dijîn.
 
These are Kurdish clothes. Children from other provinces
also live here.

198
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Bila ew jî bibînin kincê me çi ye, cilê me çi ye.
 
Let them also see what our clothes are, what our outfits
are.

199
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Û em jî bixwazin hevdû nas bikin, wek teba'dul xûbrat,
alûgorkirina çandan di navbera me û hemû pêkhateyan de.
 
And we also want to get to know each other, like exchange of
experience, exchanging cultures between us and all
components.

200
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:00,000
Çiqas em pêkhate hebin.
 
As many components as we have.

201
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,000
Spas mamoste.
 
Thank you teacher.

202
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Sax bî mamoste, sax bî.
 
Thank you teacher, thank you.

203
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Kerem bikin em bi hev re li beşên rawdeya Hêvî ya Efrînê
binêrin ...
 
Come on please let's walk.

204
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Kerem bikin em bi hev re li beşên rawdeya Hêvî ya Efrînê
binêrin ...
 
Please, let's look together at the sections of the Hevi
kindergarten of Afrin ...

205
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Zarok li kuderê dilîzin, li kuderê perwerde dibin, li kuderê
fêr dibin.
 
Where the children play, where they are trained, where they
learn.

206
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Em ê herin odeyan bibînin.
 
We will go see the rooms.

207
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Ev der, qismê tifuleta sîsî ye.
 
This place, is the early childhood section.

208
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:29,000
Ev der odeyek neşat e.
 
This is an activity room.

209
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:37,000
Zarok hinek tê de bêhna xwe fireh dikin, televîzyon heye,
dema îstîrehe tê de rûdinin.
 
Children relax a bit in it, there is a television, they sit
in it during break time.

210
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Ev odeyek zarokan a yekemîn e.
 
This is a first children's room.

211
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Zarok niha di odeyên din de ne. Berî nuha em ketine dema
îstîrehe.
 
The children are in other rooms now. We have entered the
break time just now.

212
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Ev der jî, fishe, cihê ku piştî dema wan ... piştî xwendinê.
 
This place too, break area, the place where after their time
... after studying.

213
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Zarokan derdixin da bêhna wan derkeve. Lîstok.
 
They take the children out so they can get some fresh air.
Toys.

214
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Ev havirçî, tufûleta dehiyê ye.
 
This havirçî is the childhood of the village.

215
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:17,000
Avan navê xwe çi ye?
 
What is the name of this?

216
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Qîlê.
 
Qîlê.

217
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Ev qîlê ye. Eywa.
 
This is qîlê. Yes.

218
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Keçikan dest dan hev, yek.
 
The girls held each other's hands, one.

219
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Navê wê qîlê ye.
 
Its name is qîlê.

220
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Qîlê.
 
Qîlê.

221
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Yê ku bikişîne wî alî, wê jê re çepikan lêxin, ne?
 
The one who pulls to that side, they will clap for her,
right?

222
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Aa.
 
Yes.

223
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Alîn, Alîn, Alîn!
 
Alin, Alin, Alin!

224
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Keçê bikişîne, keçê bikişîne!
 
Girl pull, girl pull!

225
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:48,000
A, destê xwe berdan...
 
Ah, they let go of their hands...

226
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,000
A, berdan...
 
Ah, they let go...

227
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:52,000
Bravo.
 
Bravo.

228
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:58,000
(Cheering)
 
(Cheering)

229
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:03,000
Hêdî, hêdî, neşkînin hev, wey.
 
Slowly, slowly, don't break each other, oh.

230
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Keçkê, neêşînin xwe!
 
Girls, don't hurt yourselves!

231
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:10,000
Tê destê xwe berde, tê destê xwe berde...
 
She will let go of her hand, she will let go of her hand...

232
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Ha xesirî! Ha xesirî!
 
Ha she lost! Ha she lost!

233
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Mizgîn, Mizgîn, Mizgîn, Mizgîn!
 
Mizgin, Mizgin, Mizgin, Mizgin!

234
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:34,000
Ehmed, were wira. Ehmed, were.
 
Ahmed, come here. Ahmed, come.

235
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Bo çi wisa... Xweş e.
 
Why like this... It's nice.

236
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Cihê xwe bigirin.
 
Take your positions.

237
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,000
Yalla, yalla.
 
Come on, come on.

238
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Ev xeta navbera we ye, aha.
 
This is the line between you, here.

239
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:45,000
Pêyekî xwe bidin pêş.
 
Put one foot forward.

240
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,000
Destê xwe bidin hev.
 
Hold each other's hands.

241
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:49,000
Baş e, we destê hevdu girt?
 
Okay, did you hold each other's hands?

242
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:52,000
Baş e, sê gav e.
 
Okay, it's three steps.

243
00:31:52,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Bisekinin ez ê niha ji we re bibêjim, yek dudu sê û dest pê
bikin.
 
Wait I will tell you now, one two three and start.

244
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Baş e? Dest pê kin!
 
Okay? Start!

245
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Na na, bisekinin.
 
No no, wait.

246
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Em ê wisa bikin. Em ê dîsa dest pê bikin.
 
We will do it like this. We will start again.

247
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Aha ne bi vî destî.
 
Aha not with this hand.

248
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:17,000
Oho na bi vî destî, na bi vî destî.
 
Oho no not with this hand, not with this hand.

249
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Aha wiha bi destê rastê...
 
Yes like this with the right hand...

250
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Aha ev yek qebûl nake.
 
Aha this one doesn't accept it.

251
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Ev dixwaze destê din bide, ev yek qebûl nake.
 
This one wants to give the other hand, this one doesn't
accept it.

252
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Yalla, yalla!
 
Come on, come on!

253
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Bikişîne, bikişîne! Yalla, yalla, bikişîne!
 
Pull, pull! Come on, come on, pull!

254
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Bravo, bravo, bravo!
 
Bravo, bravo, bravo!

255
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Hozan, Hozan, Hozan!
 
Hozan, Hozan, Hozan!

256
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Bikişîne, bikişîne, yalla, yalla!
 
Pull, pull, come on, come on!

257
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:58,000
(Cheering)
 
(Cheering)

258
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Destê xwe berda, destê xwe berda!
 
He let go of his hand, he let go of his hand!

259
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Bravo!
 
Bravo!

260
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Herin cîhê xwe, herin cîhê xwe.
 
Go to your places, go to your places.

261
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:16,000
(Chatter and background noise)
 
(Chatter and background noise)

262
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Yalla derbas bin wira.
 
Come on, pass over there.

263
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Kuro derbas be.
 
Boy, pass.

